<title>USA: Perceptron Inc Q1 net off, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Perceptron Inc Q1 net off, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, Mich. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997		1996</p>
<p> Net sales				  $ 10,330	    $ 9,510</p>
<p> Cost of sales				 4,270		3,921</p>
<p> Gross profit				  6,060		5,589</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expense		   3,198		2,801</p>
<p>Engineering, research and</p>
<p>  development expense			1,911		1,295</p>
<p> Non-cash stock compensation expense	 0		  421</p>
<p> Income from operations			951		1,072</p>
<p> Interest income, net			  182		  161</p>
<p>Income before provision for income taxes</p>
<p>						   1,133		1,233</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		  340		  374</p>
<p> Net income					793		  859</p>
<p>Net income per weighted average</p>
<p>  common share				   .10		  .11</p>
<p>Weighted average common and common</p>
<p>  equivalent shares		    8,227,543	  7,854,650</p>
<p>		  (In $000's except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Results of both periods include Autospect Inc which was acquired in February, 1997. Autospect realized a loss in the quarter of $0.04 per share, due to reduced sales levels and certain acquisition expenses. This compares to a loss of $0.01 per share in the prior year.</p>
<p>	    ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
